       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults in a monitored setting (3,200 mg/day). It would put the patient at serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory dose\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give me a clinical rationale for the order note."
