       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum labeled and studied dose. No indication I know of supports it, and the risks of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up without any added benefit. You also didn't give a clinical rationale, which I'd asked for.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within range right away.** For example, 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day) or 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day). The ceiling is 3,200 mg/day, for example 800 mg four times daily.\n- **Help with an alternative** if the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect. That could be scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen, or another agent. Your pharmacist can help choose.\n- **Route the order through pharmacy.** If you think there is a real reason for this dose, the pharmacy or clinical decision support team should review it and approve it directly.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
